### OKX-bound modules left in place (not modified; for the user to port or retire)
LIVE TRADING (VM stack, now stopped)
  research/live_scanner.py        one scan cycle: refreshes OKX bars via freqtrade --exchange okx, screens pairs, publishes candidates
  research/stop_monitor.py        tick stop monitor on the OKX public websocket; sole ledger writer
  scripts/vm_scan_cycle.sh        VM cron cycle: freqtrade download-data --exchange okx, then the scanner
  scripts/check_vm.sh             VM status wrapper; its `oi` subcommand pulls the retired OKX OI collector's files
DATA PATH
  research/data_loader.py         get_price_levels; imports adapters.okx_futures + lst_tokens (to be REPLACED in B2 by the HL adapter, per brief)
  research/universe_panel.py      panel cache + tradeable pairs; OKX only in docstrings ("212 instruments", okx_futures)
  research/intrabar.py            1m/fine log prices for exit checks; reads user_data/data/okx/futures directly
  research/validate_intrabar.py   validator for intrabar.py; prints an OKX-specific check
  research/pair_analysis.py       pair diagnostics; reads raw OKX 30m feathers directly
  research/coint_screen.py        cointegration-screened universe; reads okx/futures/*_USDT_USDT-30m directly; OKX taker cost in docstring
RESEARCH (dislocation_model)
  envelope.py                     MAE/MFE envelope; RAW_BAR_DIR + {t}_USDT_USDT-1m filenames (RAW_BAR_DIR repointed in B2, per brief)
  meta_label.py                   META-LABEL step 0; builds {t}_USDT_USDT-1m paths off envelope.RAW_BAR_DIR
  envfeat.py                      five environment features; RAW_DIR = okx/futures (30m OHLCV)
  whyfeat.py                      WHY-IT-MOVED features; RAW_DIR = okx/futures, OKX volume
  reachfeat2.py                   REACH-MU v2; perp vs OKX 1h index feathers, 1m futures
  (transitively: reachmu.py, delayed*.py, chopdrift.py, whyscreen.py, whycheck.py, reachfeat.py import from the above)
TEXT ONLY
  research/ou_model.py            OU model; "matches the OKX perpetual funding cycle" (8h) in a comment
  research/risk_sim.py            portfolio sim; "leverage than OKX allows" in docstring
CONFIG/OTHER
  .env.example, requirements.txt, user_data/config_backfill.json, .gitignore comments
